.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt MEMOBJ_CREATE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm memobj_create
.Nd create an anonymous memory object
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft Handle
.Fn memobj_create "usize len" "usize flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call creates a memory object. With a zero
.Fa flags
argument it is anonymous and zero-filled. With the
.Dv memobj::PAGER
flag the caller becomes the object's pager: no frames are allocated, the
returned handle is the pager key, and page faults are served with
.Xr pager_supply 2 .
.Pp
This page documents the native RavenBSD ABI; see the
.Pa raven-abi
crate for the exact numeric value and types.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success .Nm returns a non-negative value; on failure it returns a negative error number.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
